  "notes": "Drawn from A350-1000 photos, 2022-2026, both sides. The tessellation is simplified to its biggest facets: on the aircraft there are more, smaller triangles in several tones of gold, brown, cream and gray, and they differ a little between types. The right face's facets mirror the left's (A6-XWN). The wing's under-side and the belly are plain beige as far as the photos show. Text placements are for the left side; on the right the Arabic is still forward and the emblem aft, and the tagline is in Arabic. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on A6-XWF (left, 2022): the titles sit where drawn (within about 0.2 m); the Arabic name runs x 0.156 to 0.19, ahead of 'ETIHAD'; the Arabic tagline on the right is given about the English one's length (low: not measured). The facets are straight-edged and stay as drawn.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation (a few remembered colors, 2026-11-12). 'Facets of Abu Dhabi' replaced the first (2003) livery from September 2014; it still flies fleet-wide."
}
